+# REPORT 04 — Status DONE
+
+## Changes
+- `src/arci/runner.py` (ADR 0006): `_pythonpath` appends `os.getcwd()` last (after the parent's `sys.path` and the inherited `PYTHONPATH`) when it is not already present; never prepended, so replay's bundle directory and installed packages keep precedence. A removed cwd is skipped (`OSError` guard). Added `child_pythonpath(extra=())`, a one-line public name for `_pythonpath`, so `arci.init` can use the rule without a private import (basedpyright strict `reportPrivateUsage`).
+- `src/arci/init.py` (new): `parse_request` (in-process checks in ADR order: argument syntax incl. `--task`/`--task-file` exclusion, `--n` 1..10000, `--out` suffix; experiment id `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*`; reference syntax via the frozen AgentRef pattern; task JSON (object only, NaN/Infinity/overflow refused); `--fault NAME[:TOOL[:OCC]]` (only `tool_timeout`, `tool_error_once`, `empty_result`; TOOL omitted or empty = any tool; OCC omitted = 0); output collision (`--force` replaces only a regular file; directory, symlink (incl. dangling) and other non-regular files are never replaced; missing parent directory refused)). `check_references`: ONE child `sys.executable -P -c <script>`, env `PYTHONPATH = child_pythonpath(())`, `start_new_session=True`, 30 s deadline (`deadline=` keyword for tests), process group SIGKILLed on timeout AND after every check (no descendant survives), stdin/stdout/stderr are temp files (no pipe can stall the parent). In the child the original fd 1 is duplicated for the one JSON result line and fd 1 / `sys.stdout` point at stderr, so user prints (Python or raw fd) never mix with the result; user output is captured and discarded. The child imports each module, then `contracts.resolve` (import error / missing attribute / not callable distinguished), in order baseline, candidate, toolset, oracle; calls the toolset factory once with `(task, 0)`, reads `.tools` (a Mapping of str) and checks `.snapshot` is callable. Agents, oracle, tools and snapshot are never called; the parent never imports a reference (tested via `sys.modules`). Fault TOOLs are checked against the advertised keys. `render_descriptor`: the five-line ADR header, then keys with every string value double-quoted (PyYAML dumper with a quoted-str representer; task as a one-line flow mapping). Arms `baseline`/`candidate` with no candidate_id (Manifest default ""); task_id omitted (ruling 1: it is the experiment id); one condition `faults` (all faults in order, bucket falsify) or `clean`; `n_per_arm` default 8. `publish`: `mkstemp` beside the destination, chmod to the umask default, re-load through `compile_descriptor_text`, seal check and field round-trip check, re-check the output, then `os.link` (no `--force`: refuses an output that appeared meanwhile) or `os.replace` (`--force`); the staged file is always removed.
+- `src/arci/cli.py`, `# --- init ---` regions only: import block, `_cmd_init` (InitError -> `CliError("init: ...")`, success prints exactly `arci run <shlex-quoted out>`), the `init` subparser, dispatch.
+- `src/arci/descriptor.py`: `parse_yaml` now composes the node graph and rejects a repeated mapping key before construction: `descriptor <file>:<path to the key>: duplicate key "<k>" at line L, column C; give each key once`. Merge-key (`<<`) overrides are not duplicates; anchored nodes are visited once.
+- Fixture `tests/unit/init/fixtures/sample_project/{app/__init__.py, app/v1.py (retry, plus non-callable NAME), app/v2.py (no retry), tests/__init__.py, tests/world.py (tool `reserve`, first call times out on ~35% of seeds; `passed`)}`. No `__init__.py` in `fixtures/`, so it is not part of the repo's test package; typed, basedpyright-clean.
+- Tests: `tests/unit/runner/test_pythonpath.py` (6), `tests/unit/init/test_init.py` (40: success bytes, header, quoting, labels/task_id/n/condition, mode, faults in one condition, task/task-file, shell quoting, `--force`, the four ref error classes plus toolset import error, fault tool absent, ref order, the console-script premise, init->run e2e, all syntax errors and in-process order, directory/symlink/dangling-symlink refusal with and without `--force`, help), `tests/unit/init/test_child.py` (9: timeout kills child and grandchild, no descendant survives a successful check, user prints do not corrupt the result and nothing else is called, toolset-call / tools / snapshot / `os._exit` / `SystemExit` failures), `tests/unit/descriptor/test_descriptor.py` (+4: duplicate keys at top level, in task, in a condition; merge override allowed).
+
+## Tests
+- `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/init tests/unit/runner tests/unit/cli tests/unit/descriptor tests/unit/report tests/acceptance/test_cli.py tests/acceptance/test_runner_replay.py` -> `287 passed in 58.40s` (with `-q` the addopts `-q` makes it dots only, all dots)
+- `.venv/bin/pytest tests -x` (whole suite) -> `1035 passed, 2 skipped in 371.12s`
+- `.venv/bin/ruff format --check .` -> `277 files already formatted`; `.venv/bin/ruff check .` -> `All checks passed!`; `.venv/bin/basedpyright` -> `0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes` (no pyright ignores added)
+- `shasum -a 256 -c FROZEN.sha256 | grep -v OK` -> no output
+- `python3 docs/assets/src/make_figures.py --check` -> `figures are current: hero-dark.svg, hero-light.svg, where-dark.svg, where-light.svg`
+- Real end-to-end, fresh temp dir holding only the fixture copy, `PYTHONPATH` unset:
+  - `.venv/bin/python -P -m arci.cli init checkout-retry --baseline app.v1:run --candidate app.v2:run --toolset tests.world:make_world --oracle tests.world:passed` -> exit 0, stdout `arci run arci.yaml`, stderr empty.
+  - `.venv/bin/python -P -m arci.cli run arci.yaml` -> exit 2; stdout ends `VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2)` (baseline 8/8, candidate 7/8); stderr is the two task-05 smoke lines; `runs/checkout-retry/{manifest.json,trials.jsonl,events.jsonl,decision.json}` written.
+  - `head -8 arci.yaml`:
+    ```
+    # arci experiment descriptor. Schema: `arci schema`.
+    # smoke design: expect INCONCLUSIVE; run arci plan before a confirmatory N
+    # Default: 8 trials per arm; this scaffold does not establish confirmatory power.
+    # Plan before trials: arci plan --help
+    # Never extend this experiment based on its verdict.
+    experiment_id: "checkout-retry"
+    task: {}
+    toolset: "tests.world:make_world"
+    ```
+
+## Deviations (with reason)
+1. `runner.child_pythonpath` added beside `_pythonpath` (brief: "`_pythonpath` only"): strict basedpyright forbids importing the private name; a public alias avoids a `# pyright: ignore`.
+2. The fault-tool message appends the advertised tools: `--fault tool_timeout:charge:0: tool charge absent from --toolset tests.world:make_world; choose an advertised tool (reserve)`. The other ADR messages are verbatim (`module not importable; check module and dependencies`, `output arci.yaml exists; use --force to replace it`). Messages the ADR does not list are mine: missing attribute (`module app.v2 has no attribute runn; check the function name`), not callable (`NAME is not callable; reference a function`), toolset call/tools/snapshot failures, timeout, child exited before reporting, all syntax errors (see tests for exact lines).
+3. argparse-level errors (missing required flag, unknown flag) keep the CLI's existing `error: CliError: <argparse message>` form without the `init:` prefix: `_Parser.error` is outside my regions. Everything init validates itself carries `init:`.
+4. Added check: `--out` must end in `.yaml`/`.yml`, because `arci run` treats any other path as manifest JSON (the printed next command would fail otherwise).
+5. `NAME::OCC` (empty TOOL) is accepted as "any tool at OCC"; the ADR says only "omitted TOOL means any tool".
+6. `task_id` is not written (the loader's ruling 1 makes it the experiment id); asserted after reload.
+7. `tests/unit/descriptor/test_run_yaml.py` (T03, my lane): its `stderr == ""` assertion for an N=6 run now expects exactly the task-05 notice lines.
