+# REPORT 05 — Status DONE
+
+## Changes
+- `src/arci/cli.py`, `# --- smoke ---` regions only (one block of helpers before `_cmd_run`, two small regions inside `_cmd_run`; the descriptor region is untouched):
+  - `smoke_notice(manifest)`: fires when the manifest has at least one gating condition (no ceiling fault, as the gate counts K) and `n_per_arm < 100`; printed to stderr after the manifest loads and before `run_experiment`. In the planner's domain (clopper_pearson, K=1, looks `()` or `(n_per_arm,)`):
+    `SMOKE DESIGN: n_per_arm=<N> (alpha <a>, delta <d>, K=1): under the default rule two perfect arms cannot PASS below N=<p> and a total collapse cannot BLOCK below N=<b>; expect INCONCLUSIVE. Plan a confirmatory N: arci plan --baseline-rate P --candidate-rate P --target-verdict BLOCK`
+    with `<p>`/`<b>` the smallest N at which N/N vs N/N gives PASS and N/N vs 0/N gives BLOCK, for the manifest's own alpha/delta, computed with the gate's functions (`planning.per_arm_tail`, `stats.clopper_pearson_tail`, `stats.difference_bounds`, `gate.classify`), scanning every N from 1 to the planner bound 400 (no monotonicity assumed). If none is found: `cannot PASS at any N up to 400`. Outside the domain the numbers are the default rule's (alpha 0.05, delta 0.10), and the line says so: `... K=2): under the default rule (default rule: alpha 0.05, delta 0.1, K=1, one look; this design is outside the planner's domain) two perfect arms cannot PASS below N=42 ...`.
+  - `smoke_followup(manifest)`: after the report, only when the notice fired and the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE: `INCONCLUSIVE at n_per_arm=<N> is the expected smoke result; choose a confirmatory N with arci plan before re-running.`
+  - Nothing on stdout; reports, decision.json, stores and exit codes unchanged; `arci report`, `arci gate`, `arci plan` unchanged. Gate/planner names are imported inside the helpers so that no existing import line outside the region changes.
+- `src/arci/init.py` header (task 04) already carries the smoke comment line.
+- `tests/unit/cli/test_smoke_notice.py` (14 tests).
+
+## Tests
+- Covered: a real N=6 run (subprocess) exits 2 with stderr exactly the two lines, stdout's last line `VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2)`, stdout byte-equal to `render_markdown` over the loaded store, `arci report` stdout identical with empty stderr, `arci gate` stdout identical and `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` file equal to the Markdown, nothing in decision.json; in-process with `run_experiment` stubbed to raise, the notice appears before the run for N=6 and N=99 and not for N=100, N=200 or a ceiling-only manifest, and K counts gating conditions only; out-of-domain designs (K=2, newcombe, two looks) state the default rule, a single look equal to n_per_arm stays in domain; for (alpha, delta) in (0.05, 0.10), (0.01, 0.2), (0.1, 0.2), (0.2, 0.3) the printed thresholds agree with `planning.verdict_table` (decides at the printed N, at no smaller N); delta 0.01 prints `cannot PASS at any N up to 400`.
+- `.venv/bin/pytest tests -x` (whole suite) -> `1035 passed, 2 skipped in 371.12s`
+- Done-when selection (see report 04): `287 passed in 58.40s`; ruff format/check clean; basedpyright `0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes`; FROZEN check no output; figures current.
+- The real end-to-end in report 04 shows the two stderr lines at N=8:
+  `SMOKE DESIGN: n_per_arm=8 (alpha 0.05, delta 0.1, K=1): under the default rule two perfect arms cannot PASS below N=42 and a total collapse cannot BLOCK below N=8; expect INCONCLUSIVE. Plan a confirmatory N: arci plan --baseline-rate P --candidate-rate P --target-verdict BLOCK`
+  `INCONCLUSIVE at n_per_arm=8 is the expected smoke result; choose a confirmatory N with arci plan before re-running.`
+
+## Deviations (with reason)
+1. In-domain lines keep the dispatch's exact words "under the default rule" even when the manifest's alpha/delta are not the defaults; the numbers are then the manifest's own (alpha and delta are printed in the parentheses). "Default rule" there reads as the gate's fixed-sample Clopper-Pearson rule. Astra should confirm this wording (statistics review is mandatory).
+2. Thresholds are searched up to the planner's bound (400), not 10000: one Clopper-Pearson evaluation costs O(N^2) and a full scan to 10000 takes minutes. At or below 400 the scan is exhaustive.
+3. `tests/unit/descriptor/test_run_yaml.py` asserted empty stderr for an N=6 `arci run`; it now asserts exactly the notice lines (see report 04).
+
+## Open issues
+- At 42 <= N < 100 with default alpha/delta the line still says "expect INCONCLUSIVE" although two perfect arms can then PASS; this is the specified trigger (< 100), but the sentence is weaker there.
+- The notice is not shown by `arci gate` (allowed by the brief).
